{
 "schemaVersion": 1,
 "seedVersion": "2026-11-09.1",
 "description": "Declaration of the EU IOSS/VOEC tax-rate configuration IMS needs before it can replace Xeroom. A DECLARATION ONLY: nothing reads this file to post a document, nothing writes a tax rate to Xero from it, and it is applied to the database only by an operator running `npm run eu-vat:seed -- --apply --confirm <digest>` (dry run by default). `npm run eu-vat:preflight` compares it with the database and the stored Xero list and writes nothing.",
 "provenance": "Measured 2026-11-09: the 65 live WooCommerce tax rates, the Xeroom option xero_taxes_association resolved through xero_defined_tax_methods, and the IMS stage copy of the Xero tax-rate list. Names are byte-exact, including the double space in 'AT IOSS  VAT'. The expected posting type of every row is what Xeroom resolves it to (the parity test pins this against tests/fixtures/eu-vat-parity.json).",
 "rules": [
  "One IMS rate per WooCommerce rate (owner ruling Q2): no IMS rate is shared by two WooCommerce rates, and R13 is not exempted for the zero-rated class.",
  "accountingTaxType is the CHARGED rate's Xero code. null means: the live code is resolved by name from the stored Xero list at setup (npm run tax:rekey), never declared here, because Xero numbers custom codes per organisation.",
  "schemePostingTaxType is the zero-rated Xero type the goods, shipping and discount lines of a scheme sale post on; it is never the charged code. reportingCategory IOSS or VOEC marks the rate as sold under that scheme.",
  "Rates 223 (ES Canary Islands) and 231 (Isle of Man) are outside the scheme and carry neither field. Rate 182 posts on ZERORATEDOUTPUT, as Xeroom does (owner ruling Q4)."
 ],
